    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `ownerSegment` field to the owner response, following the codebase's established pattern for read-time derived fields (a helper class in the `mapper` package, wired into `OwnerMapper` via a `@Mapping` expression, with the field declared in `openapi.yml`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 computes `'<TIER>_<AREA>'`:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when the effective `membershipLevel` (`owner.getMembershipLevel()`, falling back to `Membership.levelOf(owner)`, matching how the mapper already exposes `membershipLevel`) is \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when `Locality.of(owner)` resolves to a known region (NSW, VIC, QLD), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` mapping expression alongside the other derived fields.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `ownerSegment` as a read-only string on the owner schema (plain `string`, consistent with sibling derived fields like `locality`/`ageBand`; an initial `enum` caused a generated typed-enum vs. `String` mismatch, so I dropped it).\n\nThe two `Cp55Tests` cases (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and the full suite is green (68/68).",
